Grainy RAW port
==============

The Rust code and C ABI shim in this crate follow the workspace MIT license.
The build-reachable source files below are bundled with their bytes unchanged.
Unused files were pruned; all licences, copyright notices and readmes from the
retained distributions remain. Compiler-forced src/native_symbols.h namespaces
zlib symbols without patching upstream sources, and includes the shared
grainy-jpeg-sys JPEG namespace header.
Generated compiler configuration headers are written only to Cargo's OUT_DIR.

Performance build (Windows MSVC): OpenMP processing regions are enabled only in
the unchanged ahd_demosaic.cpp, crx.cpp and fuji_compressed.cpp translation units.
All units compile with /openmp so the inline allocation bookkeeping has identical,
synchronized definitions. The forced src/serial_libraw.h includes those headers
before undefining LIBRAW_USE_OPENMP for every other implementation file. X-Trans
interpolation and all other processing paths therefore remain serial. Repeated
full-buffer decode hashes against the previous serial executable cover all twelve
manifest-listed CC0 cameras, three colour modes, full/half size and multiple
OMP_NUM_THREADS settings; see docs/FIELD_TEST.md. This adds the MSVC OpenMP runtime
dependency (vcomp140.dll, supplied by the Visual C++ redistributable). No vendored
source bytes or arithmetic flags are changed; non-MSVC builds remain serial.

