Unicode 15.1
  unicode_data.rs is generated from the oracle Python's Unicode 15.1
  casefold/isalnum results, so persistent camera-rule IDs do not change.
  Unicode data license: https://www.unicode.org/license.txt
  Normalization uses unicode-normalization 0.1.23 (MIT OR Apache-2.0),
  which uses the matching Unicode 15.1 normalization tables.

Additional Rust crates (licenses also accompany their crates.io packages):
  cc: MIT OR Apache-2.0
  base64: MIT OR Apache-2.0
  sha2: MIT OR Apache-2.0
  unicode-normalization: MIT OR Apache-2.0
  kamadak-exif: BSD-2-Clause
  mutate_once (kamadak-exif dependency): MIT OR Apache-2.0
  ndarray, rayon, serde, serde_json, thiserror: workspace-approved dependencies.
  ndarray-npy: MIT OR Apache-2.0; test-only access to the existing golden reader.
  grainy-cms: workspace dependency; supplies the single LittleCMS static library.
  grainy-jpeg-sys: workspace dependency; supplies the single libjpeg-turbo static
    library, headers and symbol namespace used by LibRaw's USE_JPEG path.

No GPL demosaic packs, OpenCV, Python runtime, CMake, vcpkg, NASM, or external
codec DLLs are used by this crate. OpenMP is deliberately not linked.
